zo'o pe'icai
"kamprami" is a kind of "loveability".
"puvprami" is a multistage process of getting some hormones into one's blood.
"ni prami" is the measure of (may be) the amount of the above
mentioned hormones.
"zu'o prami" is a  "ka prami" for robots.
"si'o prami" is a sceptic's "love".
"za'i prami" is a romantic's "love".
"li'i prami" - for psychologist's uses.
"mu'e parmi" is for professional "lovers".
"du'u prami" is, probably, for asking "what is love".
And "nunprami" is for somebody, who never asks "what is love" :)

"jei prami" and "su'u prami" are still waiting for explanation.


